REVISE

1. `MEDIUM` — Runtime is not driving the full phase machine, so the `VERIFY -> (EXPORT|REPAIR)` branch is currently untriggerable in live execution.
   - `BuildPhaseTracker` defines `note_finalizer_called` and `note_verifier_result` transitions (`Phase.VERIFY`, `Phase.EXPORT`, `Phase.REPAIR`) in [packages/core/src/disco/core/contract/phase.py](/var/home/dylan/projects/disco/packages/core/src/disco/core/contract/phase.py#L45).
   - Runtime composes build executors with only `on_tool_success` for the bootstrap/finalizer-to-verify edge and never forwards verifier-host outcomes ([packages/agent-server/src/disco/agent_server/runtime.py](/var/home/dylan/projects/disco/packages/agent-server/src/disco/agent_server/runtime.py#L1532) + search confirms no call sites for `note_verifier_result`/`note_finalizer_called` in runtime).
   - Effect: if/when a live verifier result is available in future or expected in flow, failed verify leaves the run stranded in `VERIFY` with repair-only paths never entered.

2. `LOW` — Per-conversation contract bookkeeping is not fully torn down on conversation deletion.
